<title>NETHERLANDS: Ceteco over-allotment option exercised.</title>
<headline>Ceteco over-allotment option exercised.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO Rothschild said on Friday the &quot;greenshoe option&quot; to cover over-allotments on the share issue of trading company and retailer Ceteco NV had been exercised by the banking syndicate backing the issue.</p>
<p>&quot;This implies that the total transaction will be increased by 86,739 non-voting shares to a total of 765,000,&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Ceteco, which is majority-owned by trading company Hagemeyer, said on April 9 it would issue the shares to finance further growth.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO later said the issue, for which the price had been set at 93 guilders per share, had been oversubscribed more than two times.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
